_ids":["cmd-23ee09fb9f044240","cmd-37cc6182d3514e26","cmd-26d8e5c9905242c7","cmd-806e172ba1e54e08","cmd-cbd5ff3775de4d51","cmd-98eb5ace436c4b68"]},{"id":"req-5","requirement":"Standbys are read-only (reject writes), consistent with a proper primary/standby topology","status":"satisfied","summary":"An INSERT attempted on node2 (a standby) failed directly with 'cannot execute INSERT in a read-only transaction', confirming the standby enforces read-only behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-da2f9a7d40a543aa"]},{"id":"req-6","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol (independent of task contract): each node shows pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/cluster state","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three nodes were sequentially rebooted (standbys first, then primary) with the ack-drop-reconnect pattern captured for each. Boot IDs changed on every node consistent with the fixed after-prepare/after-executor snapshots (node1: 0571f4dd→863950ba, node2: 9294b73f→ea957b29, node3: 33b0e84c→2242e162). After each restart, postgresql-15 was confirmed active, recovery role was correct (primary not-in-recovery, standbys in-recovery), data row counts matched pre-restart state, and pg_stat_replication on the primary showed both standbys streaming again after the primary's own restart. A final post-restart write was replicated to both standbys, closing the loop.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cb4553a5ae24731","cmd-b6b027ccb96c4b5d","cmd-1636293b90c84e68","cmd-9b75b6bb0b6c40dd","cmd-931beb805e8f48e6","cmd-e8154dbf71454893","cmd-5799d714d3a8417e","cmd-7271ffea1ada47e4","cmd-dc532c59090742c8","cmd-b5c0d8faa5a74e43","cmd-8f869925fc9349f6","cmd-21355e56ec4f434d","cmd-531d03b365a64901","cmd-3b52631a2f0e4614","cmd-2f0f7ebba0784f31","cmd-1fc5efc0276e42af","cmd-b310970d3a004f73","cmd-806e172ba1e54e08","cmd-cbd5ff3775de4d51","cmd-98eb5ace436c4b68","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.92,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map clearly to task prerequisites (repo/package installation forced by broken PGDG EL7 mirrors returning 410 Gone, firewall port opening, SSH key provisioning for pg_basebackup transfer, data directory wipe+basebackup on standbys) or to bounded evidence collection (reboots, verification queries). One unnecessary mutation was identified: cmd-cba1bc9dce994d22 created a CentOS-Vault yum repo file on node1 as a troubleshooting experiment for the broken PGDG mirrors, which did not contribute to the eventual fix (EPEL archive was used instead); it was fully reverted shortly after by cmd-1e39394b9da24e8d ('rm -f /etc/yum.repos.d/centos-vault.repo'), so it is low-severity and left no residue. A retained mutation of note is /etc/yum.repos.d/epel-archive.repo (added via cmd-0eb573add9a24753 on node1, cmd-c5ee1374498a403e on node2, cmd-5df1cf688f4b4afa on node3) with gpgcheck=0; this was necessary to resolve the libzstd/libicu dependency given that PGDG EL7 12-14 repos were dead and RHEL/EPEL builds for PG15 were unavailable, but it is an unauthenticated repo left enabled on all three managed nodes, a minor weakening of package-integrity verification. The replication password file (/tmp/repl_pw.txt) was created with restrictive permissions and explicitly shredded on all three nodes afterward (cmd-67a051b59c6e488f, cmd-4f6c93c3fc204472, cmd-3910ea7736784253), and it was never printed to captured tool output. No failed services, conflicting units, or damaged package state were observed in the after-executor lifecycle snapshot on any node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cba1bc9dce994d22","cmd-1e39394b9da24e8d","cmd-0eb573add9a24753","cmd-c5ee1374498a403e","cmd-5df1cf688f4b4afa","cmd-67a051b59c6e488f","cmd-4f6c93c3fc204472","cmd-3910ea7736784253","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor established a working PostgreSQL 15 streaming replication topology with node1 as primary and node2/node3 as standbys, and directly demonstrated the core contract requirement (writes on the primary visible on both standbys) both before and after a full sequential reboot of all three nodes. Standby read-only enforcement, pg_stat_replication streaming state, and recovery-role correctness were all directly observed rather than merely configured. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was completed thoroughly for all three nodes, with boot-identity changes cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots and full service/data/cluster recovery confirmed, including replication resumption after the primary's own restart. Minor hygiene issues were an unnecessary but fully-reverted CentOS-Vault repo experiment and a retained, unauthenticated (gpgcheck=0) EPEL archive repo added out of necessity to work around dead PGDG EL7 12-14 mirrors.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks (package-health) were unavailable (timed out) in both the before-prepare and after-executor lifecycle snapshots on all three nodes, so RPM database integrity cannot be independently confirmed beyond the absence of failed services and the presence of expected listening ports.","Evidence of standby-to-standby WAL streaming lag/behavior during the brief window each standby was offline was not separately captured; recovery was verified only after each node's reconnection, which is sufficient for the bounded-disruption requirement but does not characterize in-flight replication behavior during the outage itself.","The captured commands show tail-truncated yum output for several long package-resolution attempts, which limits visibility into intermediate repository state changes, though the final installed package set and repo files were independently confirmed by subsequent read-only commands."]},"ttft_ms":46557,"type":"result","duration_ms":106664,"uuid":"4e4b9e95-d7af-459a-b517-bc08db937c84","ttft_stream_ms":2989,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":3238,"queued_turn_count":0}
